**How to implement.** The Material editor window takes its category store from its caller, so no product code builds a self-seeding store (the S1.7 brief: the self-seeding `CategoryProxy.createInMemory` goes; .spec-md §3.3). The product's one opener already passes the shared store (`MaterialsWindow.fs:70`, `categories = categories`), and it keeps doing so, now to the mandatory parameter. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs`: the optional `?categories : CategoryProxy` constructor parameter becomes the mandatory third parameter `categories : CategoryProxy`, and the constructor's `defaultArg categories (CategoryProxy.createInMemory (fun _ -> []))` and the comment describing that default are deleted; the context takes `categories` directly. The class doc names the parameter in no more words. (2) Every test that opens the window without a store passes `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore (fun _ -> [])` (step 45), which holds what the deleted default held: `EmbeddedChartTests`, `MaterialEditorWindowTests`, `MaterialsWindowTests`, `SampleEditorWindowTests`, `ScrollExtentTests`, `WireUi0040CompositionTests` and `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`; a test that already passes a store keeps it. Every fact keeps its name and its assertions.

**Acceptance.** After the change, `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs` MUST NOT name `createInMemory` or `defaultArg categories`; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes with their counts unchanged; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.
